{"type":"message","id":"64b0983b","parentId":"8d1a4c27","timestamp":"2026-03-08T10:06:26.979Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 11:06 GMT+1] Analyze this 4 OpenClaw architecture improvements with actual code context:\n\nCURRENT IMPLEMENTATIONS:\n\n## Feature 1: Batch Memory Storage\n- Code: neuro-memory-bridge.ts + event-mesh.ts  \n- Problem: Every storeMemory() calls Python process immediately\n- During high activity, sequential IPC calls overwhelm Python process\n- Proposed: Batch with debouncing (queue memories, flush every 10 items or 100ms)\n\n## Feature 2: Event Table Partitioning\n- Code: event-mesh.ts\n- Problem: Single agent_events table grows unbounded\n- Proposed: Monthly partitioned tables with 3-month retention\n\n## Feature 3: Adaptive Compaction Thresholds\n- Code: answer-briefing-tracker.ts\n- Problem: Fixed 40 answers threshold ignores model context windows\n- Proposed: Model-aware thresholds (70% context usage, semantic density)\n\n## Feature 4: Parallel Tool Execution\n- Code: tool-execution-wrapper.ts\n- Problem: Multiple independent tools execute sequentially\n- Proposed: Dependency graph parallel execution\n\nPlease analyze each feature:\n1. Feasibility assessment (Easy/Medium/Hard)\n2. Risk level (Low/Medium/High)\n3. Potential issues or edge cases\n4. Recommended implementation order\n5. Code implementation suggestions"}],"timestamp":1772964386978}}
